const claudeCode = `# CLAUDE.md

Guidance for Claude Code in this repo. Everything here is loaded into context
on every session, so keep it short and keep it true.

## Project at a glance
- pnpm monorepo. Packages live in \`packages/*\`, deployables in \`apps/*\`.
- TypeScript everywhere, Postgres through Drizzle. No hand-written migrations.
- Astro marketing site, Fastify API, background worker.

## Commands
- Install        \`pnpm install\`
- Dev server     \`pnpm dev\`
- Typecheck      \`pnpm typecheck\`
- Unit tests     \`pnpm test\`
- What CI runs   \`pnpm check\`

Always use \`pnpm check\` before saying a task is done. Do not call \`vitest\`
directly — the wrapper sets the test environment.

## Working agreements
- Read the file and its neighbours before editing. Match what is already there.
- Edit an existing file rather than creating a near-duplicate.
- Smallest change that solves the problem. No drive-by refactors, no
  reformatting of untouched lines, no unrelated dependency bumps.
- Comments explain why, never what. A comment restating the line below it is a
  deletion, not a contribution.
- If the plan changes materially, say so before you keep going.

## Code style
- TypeScript strict. No \`any\` — use \`unknown\` plus a narrowing guard.
- Prefer \`type\` over \`interface\` unless you are extending something.
- Named exports everywhere. Early return over nested conditionals.
- Errors are values in \`packages/core\`, thrown only at the process boundary.
- Never swallow an error with an empty \`catch\`. Log it or rethrow it.

## Tests are part of the change
- Any behaviour change ships with a test in the same commit.
- Bug fix: add the test that fails without the fix, named after the bug.
- Never weaken, skip, or delete a test to get to green. If a test is wrong,
  say so explicitly and change it in its own commit.
- Report the real command output. Never claim a suite passed that you did not run.

## Commits and branches
- Conventional Commits: feat, fix, docs, refactor, test, chore, ci, build.
- Subject 72 characters max, imperative mood, no trailing period.
- One logical change per commit. Branch as feat/<slug> or fix/<slug>.
- Write the commit message only when asked.

## Hard limits — do not cross
- NEVER read, print, or edit \`.env\`, \`.env.*\`, \`*.pem\`, or anything matching
  \`*secret*\` or \`*credential*\`.
- NEVER run \`git push\`, \`git push --force\`, \`git reset --hard\`,
  \`git rebase -i\`, \`git clean\`, or \`git commit\`.
- NEVER commit directly to \`main\`, and never rewrite a pushed commit.
- NEVER edit generated output: \`dist/\`, \`.next/\`, \`**/*.gen.ts\`, or any file
  carrying a \`// generated\` header.
- NEVER add a production dependency without asking first.
- If a task genuinely needs one of the above, stop and tell me instead.

## Deeper reference
Full conventions: @docs/engineering/style-guide.md
Test matrix: @docs/engineering/testing.md`;

const codexCode = `# AGENTS.md

Read before any work in this repo.

How this file reaches Codex: Codex concatenates the AGENTS.md files it finds
from the project root down to the directory it was started in, and deeper
files win. One file per directory, and \`AGENTS.override.md\` takes precedence
over \`AGENTS.md\`. Combined guidance is capped by \`project_doc_max_bytes\`,
32 KiB by default — anything past the cap is silently dropped, so keep this
file well under that.

## Layout
- \`apps/web\`        Next.js dashboard, TypeScript
- \`apps/api\`        Fastify service, TypeScript
- \`packages/core\`   domain logic, must stay free of I/O
- \`infra/terraform\` never edit by hand — change and run \`make tf-plan\`
- \`scripts/\`        repo automation, safe to run

## Build, test, lint
- Setup:   \`make bootstrap\` (toolchain plus \`pnpm install\`)
- Unit:    \`make test\` — always this wrapper, never the raw test binary. It
           sets the environment and picks the smallest affected package.
- Scope:   \`make test -p <package>\` for one package.
- Lint:    \`make fix\` formats and lints. Do not re-run tests after it.
- Full suite: ask me first. It builds the whole matrix and is slow.

## How to make a change
1. Read the target file and its tests before editing anything.
2. Match the existing pattern. Do not introduce a fourth way of doing a thing
   that three files already do the same way.
3. Make the smallest change that solves the problem.
4. Run \`make fix\`, then \`make test -p <package>\`.
5. Report what changed and what you verified, with real command output.

## Style
- TypeScript strict, no \`any\`. \`unknown\` plus a guard.
- Named exports; no default exports outside entrypoints.
- Return a discriminated union from \`packages/core\`, throw at the boundary.
- Comments explain why, never what.

## Tests
- A behaviour change without a test is an incomplete change.
- Bug fix: failing test first, then the fix.
- Never delete or skip a test to reach green. If a test is genuinely wrong,
  fix it in its own commit and call it out in the summary.

## Commits
- Conventional Commits: feat, fix, refactor, docs, test, chore, ci, build.
- Subject 72 characters max, imperative, no trailing period.
- One concern per commit. Update the PR description when you add commits.

## Sandboxing and safety
- Assume workspace-write sandboxing: any command reaching the network or
  leaving the workspace needs explicit approval.
- NEVER read or write \`.env\`, \`.env.*\`, \`*.pem\`, or \`**/credentials*\`.
  Pull secrets at runtime with \`op run -- <cmd>\`, never inline a value.
- NEVER \`git push\`, \`git push --force\`, \`git reset --hard\`, \`git rebase -i\`,
  or \`git clean\`. Never commit on \`main\`.
- NEVER edit generated files: \`**/*.gen.ts\`, \`**/schema.sql\`, \`dist/\`.
- Ask before: adding a dependency, changing CI, touching \`infra/terraform\`,
  running a migration, or anything that deletes data.

## Keep this file alive
When you get something wrong because a rule here was missing or stale, fix
this file in the same change. A wrong rule costs more than a missing one.`;

const cursorCode = `# .cursorrules — repo root

Cursor reads this file in every conversation in this project. Newer Cursor
versions prefer scoped \`.cursor/rules/*.mdc\` files (second block below) and
Cursor also reads \`AGENTS.md\` directly, but this file is still the one
Cursor's \`/init\` looks for, so keep it working.

## Stack
- Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, Tailwind, Postgres with Drizzle.
- pnpm only. npm and yarn are not used in this repository.

## Commands
- \`pnpm dev\`        dev server on :3000
- \`pnpm typecheck\`  tsc --noEmit
- \`pnpm lint\`       eslint + prettier check
- \`pnpm test\`       vitest
- \`pnpm check\`      what CI runs — use this before asking for review

## Rules
- Read before you write. Match the file you are editing.
- Smallest change that works. No drive-by refactors, no reformatting.
- No \`any\`. Prefer \`type\` over \`interface\`. Named exports.
- Server Components by default; add \`"use client"\` only for state or handlers.
- Every fetch goes through \`src/lib/api.ts\`. Never call \`fetch\` inline.
- New component: colocate its test, its types, and its styles.

## Tests
- New behaviour ships with a test in the same commit.
- Bug fix: add the failing test first, then fix it.
- Run \`pnpm check\` before you call it done, and paste the real output.

## Git
- Conventional Commits, imperative mood, 72 characters max.
- Branch as \`feat/<slug>\` or \`fix/<slug>\`. Never commit to \`main\`.
- Never force push, never \`git reset --hard\`, never amend a pushed commit.

## Never
- Never read, write, or paste \`.env\`, \`.env.*\`, or \`*.pem\`.
- Never stage \`.env\`, \`secrets/\`, or \`node_modules/\`.
- Never run \`git push\` or \`git commit\` unless I ask.
- Never edit \`dist/\`, \`.next/\`, or any file with a \`// generated\` header.
- Never add a dependency without asking.`;

