const opencodeCode = `# AGENTS.md

One rules file, many agents. This file is read by OpenCode, Codex, Cursor,
Aider, goose, Zed and friends, so keep it tool-neutral and say nothing here
that only makes sense for one of them.

## Project
- TypeScript + Fastify, pnpm workspaces, Postgres with Drizzle.
- \`apps/api\` service, \`apps/web\` dashboard, \`packages/core\` domain logic with
  no I/O, \`scripts/\` repo automation.
- Node 22 minimum. ESM only, no CommonJS in new files.

## Commands
- Install       \`pnpm install\`
- Dev           \`pnpm dev\`
- Test          \`pnpm test\`
- Typecheck     \`pnpm typecheck\`
- Everything CI runs: \`pnpm check\`

## Working agreements
- Read the file and its tests before editing.
- Smallest change that solves the problem. No drive-by refactors.
- Prefer editing over creating. No near-duplicate helpers.
- Comments explain why, never what.
- If the plan changes, say so before continuing.

## Style
- TypeScript strict, no \`any\`, named exports, early returns.
- \`type\` over \`interface\` unless extending.
- Return a result union from \`packages/core\`; throw only at the boundary.
- Format and lint are automated. Do not hand-format.

## Tests
- Behaviour change ships with a test. Bug fix: failing test first.
- Never delete or skip a test to get green.
- Report real output from \`pnpm check\`.

## Commits
- Conventional Commits, imperative, 72 characters max, one concern each.
- Branch \`feat/<slug>\` or \`fix/<slug>\`. Never commit to \`main\`.

## Hard limits
- NEVER read, print, or edit \`.env\`, \`.env.*\`, \`*.pem\`, or any path matching
  \`*secret*\` or \`*credential*\`.
- NEVER run \`git push\`, \`git push --force\`, \`git reset --hard\`,
  \`git clean\`, or \`git commit\`.
- NEVER edit generated files: \`dist/\`, \`**/*.gen.ts\`, \`**/schema.sql\`.
- NEVER add a production dependency without asking.
- NEVER delete or overwrite files outside the repo working tree.

## Monorepo
Package-specific rules belong in a nested \`AGENTS.md\` inside the package.
Agents that walk the tree merge them from the root down; the nearest file
wins. Keep the root file about the things that are true everywhere.

## Maintenance
Every time an agent gets something wrong because this file was silent, fix it
here in the same change. Stale rules are worse than no rules.`;

