const geminiCode = `# GEMINI.md

Context for the Gemini CLI. \`/memory show\` prints everything actually loaded
this session and \`/memory reload\` re-scans after you edit a context file — run
it whenever Gemini seems to be ignoring a rule. An empty or unread context
file is the usual cause.

## Share the rules instead of duplicating them
This repo's working agreements live in \`AGENTS.md\`, which OpenCode, Codex and
Cursor read as well. Import it instead of copying it, so one edit lands
everywhere:

@AGENTS.md

Everything below is Gemini-CLI-specific.

## Project facts
- TypeScript + Fastify, pnpm workspaces, Postgres with Drizzle.
- \`apps/api\` is the service, \`apps/web\` the dashboard, \`packages/core\` holds
  domain logic and must stay free of I/O.
- \`pnpm dev\` needs \`pnpm db:seed\` first on a fresh clone.
- \`pnpm check\` is exactly what CI runs.

## Extra rules for this repo
- Keep every shell command non-interactive. Never use a command that waits
  for input, a pager, or a credential prompt.
- Prefer machine-readable output flags, e.g. \`--output json\`, so results can
  be parsed instead of scraped.
- When a task touches more than three packages, write the plan out and get
  my confirmation before editing files.
- Do not restructure the workspace to make a task easier.
- Do not add dependencies to make a build pass.

## Never
- Never read or write \`.env\`, \`.env.*\`, \`*.pem\`, or \`**/credentials*\`.
- Never run \`git push --force\`, \`git reset --hard\`, \`git clean\`, or \`rm -rf\`
  outside a temp directory.
- Never run a migration against anything except the local database.
- Never print secrets, tokens, or connection strings in output.
- Never commit. Stage what you changed and tell me what to commit.`;

